  "source": {
    "id": "essay-the-worlds-broken-what-do-we-do",
    "kind": "long-form",
    "body": "I used to think that if I attempted to make a difference, I would only make that pain worse. There is so much disappointment in the world.\nBut it turns out I was making the pain worse by not doing anything at all.\nBut this work is aligned with a part of me that has been wanting to come alive.\nDoing the work at all turned out to be its own reward. Not because the problems are solved. Not because success is guaranteed. Because it has helped me feel more connected to the kind of person I wanted to become.",
    "originRef": "obsidian:The world's broken. What do we do?#L187,L189,L200,L222",
